WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.715
Sometimes we need the reverse: start from the elements and find r and v in E C I.

00:00:05.715 --> 00:00:08.960
It takes two steps, and the first one is easy.

00:00:09.293 --> 00:00:12.999
In the perifocal frame the orbit is flat.

00:00:12.999 --> 00:00:21.133
The position is r cosine theta, r sine theta, zero, where r comes from the orbit equation.

00:00:21.527 --> 00:00:26.838
The velocity is mu over h, times minus sine theta, e plus cosine theta, zero.

00:00:26.838 --> 00:00:30.287
That's the hodograph result from the last chapter.

00:00:30.627 --> 00:00:46.307
For the Molniya at theta equals two eighty: p is eleven thousand nine hundred seventy four kilometers, h is sixty nine thousand eighty six, and r is ten thousand six hundred nine.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:01:02.560
So the position is one thousand eight hundred forty two, minus ten thousand four hundred forty eight, zero kilometers, and the velocity is five point six eight two, five point two seven eight, zero kilometers per second.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:06.325
Step two: rotate into E C I.

00:01:06.325 --> 00:01:13.827
The rows of C P N are p hat, q hat and h hat, so going back uses the transpose.

00:01:14.104 --> 00:01:21.313
In words: r is its p component times p hat, plus its q component times q hat.

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:26.744
The transpose just adds those arrows in E C I coordinates.

00:01:27.038 --> 00:01:35.939
Multiply it out, and we get nine thousand thirty one, minus five thousand three hundred seventeen, minus one thousand six hundred forty seven kilometers.

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:42.398
The velocity comes out minus two point eight six four, five point one one one, minus five point zero eight one.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:49.171
Those are exactly the measured r and v we started from.

00:01:49.171 --> 00:01:50.691
The round trip closes.

00:01:50.971 --> 00:01:51.778
Your turn.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:59.611
Pause here and do checkpoint five point one: take your practice orbit's elements back to r and v.

00:02:03.238 --> 00:02:06.775
And here's why elements are worth the trouble.

00:02:06.775 --> 00:02:11.696
To move the satellite forward in time, five numbers stay frozen.

00:02:11.696 --> 00:02:15.156
Only theta advances, using Kepler's equation.

00:02:15.156 --> 00:02:18.078
Then one rotation gives r and v again.
